g early here, considering that we\u0027re still calling `digestUtil.compute`?","I find myself asking the same question. This went through a number of iterations, as I discovered more and more requirements that incrementally eliminated any kind of potential optimisation.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m going to close this. There is room for improvement in the bytestream uploader (I had a stab at some in #23252 but hit a NPE I could not track down, at face value the area seems like it would benefit from a refactor and perhaps alignment across full and minimal upload modes).","FWIW, I don\u0027t think the uploader should be digesting files at all; all output files have already been digested (and the digests cached in memory as a `FileArtifactValue`) during action execution, so we should figure out a way to plumb that data into the uploader.","Some spawn intermediate outputs might not be stored, though."],"path":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","id":20501,"created_at":"2024-08-30T11:55:02Z","original_position":34,"side":"RIGHT","position":34,"original_start_line":202,"submitted_on_commit":"ab672a32fa3004d4c14790dd571f1b9379d9201b","diff_hunk":"@@ -201,6 +199,29 @@ public DigestFunction.Value getDigestFunction() {\n   private PathMetadata readPathMetadata(Path path, LocalFile file) throws IOException {\n     DigestUtil digestUtil \u003d new DigestUtil(xattrProvider, path.getFileSystem().getDigestFunction());\n \n+    if (remoteBuildEventUploadMode \u003d\u003d RemoteBuildEventUploadMode.MINIMAL) {\n+      // Omit all unimportant paths\n+      if (!(\n+        // Logs (regex needed for test logs as they lack a dedicated `LocalFileType`)\n+        TEST_LOG_PATTERN.matcher(path.getPathString()).matches()\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.LOG\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.PERFORMANCE_LOG\n+        // std(out|err)\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.STDOUT\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.STDERR\n+      )) {\n+        return new PathMetadata(\n+            path,\n+            digestUtil.compute(path),\n+            /* directory\u003d */ false,\n+            /* symlink\u003d */ false,\n+            /* remote\u003d */ false,\n+            /* omitted\u003d */ true,\n+            /* isBuildToolLog\u003d */ false,\n+            digestUtil.getDigestFunction());\n+      }\n+    }","submitted_start_line":202,"submitted_line":223},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The removal of `BUILD_LOG_PATTERN` and the associated logic in `isBuildOrTestLog` method can lead to incorrect behavior if there are build logs that do not match the `TEST_LOG_PATTERN`. The new logic in `readPathMetadata` relies solely on `LocalFileType`, which might not cover all cases where build logs need to be identified. Consider reintroducing or refining the pattern matching for build logs.","nodes":[{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-10630:10845-","promptId":"#FZN8H","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10630,"endPos":10845,"startLine":296,"startLineOffset":2,"endLine":299,"endLineOffset":3,"length":216}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-10449:10602-","promptId":"#VFJ6X","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10449,"endPos":10602,"startLine":289,"startLineO